# Code Style & Formatting

- Use English for all code and documentation
- Always declare types (variables, function parameters, return values)
- Avoid `any`, create necessary types instead
- Use JSDoc for public classes and methods
- No blank lines within functions
- One export per file

# Naming Conventions

- PascalCase: classes, components
- camelCase: variables, functions, methods
- kebab-case: files, directories
- UPPERCASE: environment variables
- Define constants instead of magic numbers

# Functions & Logic

- Keep functions short (<20 lines) and single-purpose
- Avoid nesting with early returns and utility functions
- Use higher-order functions (map, filter, reduce)
- Arrow functions for simple cases (<3 instructions), named functions otherwise
- Use default parameter values instead of null/undefined checks
- Use RO-RO (Receive Object, Return Object) pattern

# Data Handling

- Encapsulate data in composite types over primitive types
- Use classes with internal validation instead of validation in functions
- Prefer immutability: `readonly` properties, `as const` for literals

# Project Structure

## Components `/src/components/`

- Reusable UI components, presentation-focused
- Minimal dependencies, configurable via props
- Define complex prop types in separate `type/*.type.ts`

## Shadcn Components `/src/components/ui`

- Use ShadCN components defined in this folder in ALL circumstances.
- Components in this folder has the highest priority to be used.
- These components are defined by ShadCN. Under no circumstances should you change the content of any file inside this folder.


## API `/src/api/`

- Use configured `apiClient` for backend requests
- Structure: `client/index.ts`, `client/customFetch.ts`, service files

## Assets `/src/assets/`

- Images, fonts, icons in appropriate subdirectories
- Use consistent naming, optimize file sizes

## Constants `/src/constants/`

- Store static values (API routes, action types)

## Contexts `/src/contexts/`

- Global state providers and shared logic

## Hooks `/src/hooks/`

- Custom hooks for reusable logic
- Use the package `react-query` for all API calls. useQuery for GET calls and useMutation for POST calls.
- Prefix with `use`, return objects not arrays

## Layouts `/src/layouts/`

- Page structure components (headers, footers, navigation)

## Locales `/src/locales/`

- Translation files by language
- DO NOT hard code text inside any pages or components. 
- Instead, after you have created the UI, create the appropriate translations inside the folder of our two main language `/src/locales/en` and `/src/locales/zh`
- Please always check if both language has the same structure and the list of keys. And after everything, the text in the UI should be using t() function.

## Reducers `/src/reducers/`

- State management reducers

## Routes `/src/routes/`

- Route configuration with lazy loading

## Stores `/src/stores/`

- Recoil atoms and selectors

## Styles `/src/styles/`

- Global styles, themes, utilities

## Types `/src/types/`

- TypeScript types, interfaces

## Utils `/src/utils/`

- Utility functions

## Pages `/src/pages/`

- Page components using file system routing

# Best Practices

## File Naming & Structure

- PascalCase for components (.tsx)
- camelCase for utilities (.ts)
- Consistent component structure with typed props

## Imports

- Use `@/` alias for absolute imports
- Order: React, third-party, internal, styles

## Testing

- Add `data-testid` to important components

## Variables

- Use semantic names for sizes: xsmall, small, normal, medium, large, xlarge
- For all tailwind colors, always use the colors defined in `colorTheme.ts`. Do not use color + number, such as blue-[100], instead, use primary